        "model_description": "VibeVoice is a long-form, multi-speaker text-to-speech model from Microsoft Research. The 1.5B variant can synthesise up to 90 minutes of conversational speech with up to 4 distinct speakers via 'Speaker N:' scripts and per-speaker WAV reference audio. The original Microsoft repository removed the TTS inference code in Sept 2025; this engine loads the model via the maintained community fork at vibevoice-community/VibeVoice. Output is 24 kHz mono WAV. Apache/MIT licenses for code; Microsoft Research license for weights."
